                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The series has always had an issue with not making it clear what the single sentence decisions mean because more often than not depending on how you read it an option could in theory be what you'd hope to get, only for your attunement to lower.\n\nNow you're adding a whole detective portion in the beginning, followed by an extremely long portion after that which I didn't care for. With no save points this means I slowly saw the punishing system where one mistake is worth way more than a solid choice, and my attunement kept lowering. This is too much. The other novels' shorter length was fine with this system since ultimately I could retry portions to keep my score high, but now I am not about to replay ALL of this to teach the point I am in. Particularly when what I'm reading isn't necessarily something I'm enjoying.",
